course: dictionary
lesson: 3020
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Dictionaries list them as numbered meanings. Dynamite can be a noun for a powerful explosive, a verb meaning to blow something up, or slang for something exciting. The words around it show you which meaning is meant.
explain: If a sentence talks about rock, mines, fuses or blasting, dynamite means the explosive. Only trained experts should handle it, because it is very dangerous. Ask yourself: would this sentence make sense as a real explosion? If yes, use the explosive meaning.
explain: «That news is dynamite» does not mean the news explodes. Here the word is slang for something amazing or very exciting. When the meaning seems strange, try the other meanings in the sentence and see which one fits best.
fact: Dynamite is a powerful explosive, made in sticks.
fact: Alfred Nobel invented dynamite in 1867, and later left his money to start the Nobel Prizes.
fact: As a verb, «dynamite» means to blow something up with dynamite.
fact: In slang, «dynamite» means something very exciting, powerful or likely to cause big trouble.
fact: «Dynamite» is also the title of a pop song by BTS, which reached number one on the Billboard Hot 100 in 2020.
exercise: «The miners used dynamite to blast through the hard rock.» What does dynamite mean here? | Very exciting news | *A powerful explosive | A small red candle | A type of pop song
exercise: «That news is dynamite!» What does dynamite mean in this sentence? | To blow something up | A stick of explosive | *Something amazing and exciting | A kind of rock
exercise: «Engineers dynamited the old bridge before the new one was built.» Find and copy the word that shows an action, the verb form of dynamite. | bridge | Engineers | *dynamited | old
test: «The fuse fizzed as the dynamite was lit.» What does dynamite mean? | A pop song | A sweet treat | *A powerful explosive | Very boring news
test: «Her goal in the final match was dynamite!» What does dynamite mean here? | A kind of rock found in mines | *Something thrilling and amazing | A stick of explosive that is lit | To blow something up with dynamite
exam: «The town council wants to dynamite the old tower.» What does dynamite mean here? | Very old | *To blow something up | A pop song | A sweet treat
